{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And by the spirit</b> of YHWH — in the Masorah here and elsewhere: וברוח שפתיו ימית רשע. And 'וברוח' is defective (בער). For by His spirit He kills the wicked and burns them up (מבערם). And elsewhere: וברוח פיו כל צבאם — these He burns up by spirit, and those He creates by spirit:" "<b>בלב ים</b> — three times in the Masorah: בלב ים (here), דרך אניה בלב ים, והיו כשוכב בלב ים. Israel walked through the sea on a straight and level path like the way of a ship in the heart of the sea, as written: דרך לעבור גאולים. But the Egyptians walked frantically with no path, and they were כשוכב בלב ים:"], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The word בער likely signals that וברוח is written deficiently (without a vav); the phrase also carries the semantic thread of בער 'burn/consume' linking to the punishment theme."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:05.049495418Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}